umber":"FKX167","desc":"Fort Knox Recordings celebrated 20 years of releasing funky music In 2023, opening the vaults and inviting a new wave of producers to remix some of their classic catalog tracks. The response was overwhelming, and with continued interest, weve reopened those vaults once again. Next up in the remix series is a surefire dance floor burner: Takimba \u0026 Maxwell Cuttys fresh take on the Fort Knox Five classic, The Spirit of 75.\n\nThe Portland, Oregon-based duo, Takimba \u0026 Maxwell Cutty, have been making waves with their bumping, funk-fueled house tracks—including last years standout release, Kickin It. Takimba is known for his genre-blending sets that fuse funk, soul, hip-hop, and global rhythms, while Maxwell Cutty crafts genre-defying sonic hybrids that merge house, techno, funk, and experimental sounds. Together, theyve combined their distinct styles to flip the retro breakbeat energy of The Spirit of 75 into a funky tech-house monster.\n\nFort Knox Fives music has always been timeless and incredibly funky—one foot in the past and another in the future, says Jo Takimba. This is one of the first tracks we fell in love with over a decade ago. It came out in 2008 but pays homage to vibes and esthetic from 1970s soundtracks and chase scenes. We wanted to take things even further into the future bringing it to the dance floors of 2025 and beyond with a focus on the powerful message that is more relevant today than ever!\n\nThe T\u0026MC remix incorporates the high-energy groove, tight breakbeats, funky bass lines, and vibrant horn sections of the original—but turns up the heat with driving four-on-the-floor beats and modern production flair. Its a bold tribute to the classic track, reimagined through a contemporary electronic lens. Expect this one to be booming across festival stages all summer long.\n\nRadio mix and instrumental included.","enabled":true,"encoded_date":"2025-06-19T15:01:02-06:00","exclusive":false,"id":5140403,"image":{"id":